WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.141
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.441 --> 00:00:09.211
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.511 --> 00:00:14.671
Unit five: Eating Out. Today you will order food politely with would like and would prefer.

4
00:00:14.971 --> 00:00:17.612
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:22.078
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.917 --> 00:00:24.080
Reservation.

7
00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:28.000
Reservation means booking a table in advance.

8
00:00:28.617 --> 00:00:30.930
We made a reservation for six people.

9
00:00:31.517 --> 00:00:34.506
Your turn. Say: Reservation.

10
00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:38.507
Reservation.

11
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:39.972
Menu.

12
00:00:40.983 --> 00:00:43.354
Menu means a list of food you can order.

13
00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:45.532
Can I see the menu, please?

14
00:00:46.117 --> 00:00:48.467
Your turn. Say: Menu.

15
00:00:51.333 --> 00:00:52.172
Menu.

16
00:00:52.917 --> 00:00:53.744
Waiter.

17
00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.690
Waiter means a person who serves food in a restaurant.

18
00:00:58.283 --> 00:00:59.900
The waiter brought our drinks.

19
00:01:00.483 --> 00:01:02.590
Your turn. Say: Waiter.

20
00:01:05.433 --> 00:01:06.283
Waiter.

21
00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:08.005
Appetizer.

22
00:01:09.017 --> 00:01:11.980
Appetizer means a small dish before the main meal.

23
00:01:12.583 --> 00:01:15.175
We ordered spring rolls as an appetizer.

24
00:01:15.783 --> 00:01:18.796
Your turn. Say: Appetizer.

25
00:01:21.633 --> 00:01:22.843
Appetizer.

26
00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:24.817
Main course.

27
00:01:25.817 --> 00:01:28.385
Main course means the biggest dish of a meal.

28
00:01:28.983 --> 00:01:31.169
For the main course, I'll have fish amok.

29
00:01:31.783 --> 00:01:34.354
Your turn. Say: Main course.

30
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.422
Main course.

31
00:01:39.183 --> 00:01:40.068
Dessert.

32
00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:43.501
Dessert means sweet food at the end of a meal.

33
00:01:44.117 --> 00:01:46.639
Mango sticky rice is my favorite dessert.

34
00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:50.135
Your turn. Say: Dessert.

35
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:53.722
Dessert.

36
00:01:54.483 --> 00:01:55.159
Tip.

37
00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:58.486
Tip means extra money for good service.

38
00:01:59.083 --> 00:02:01.187
We left a tip for the friendly waiter.

39
00:02:01.783 --> 00:02:04.250
Your turn. Say: Tip.

40
00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:07.672
Tip.

41
00:02:08.417 --> 00:02:09.151
Bill.

42
00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:12.707
Bill means a paper showing how much to pay.

43
00:02:13.317 --> 00:02:15.038
Could we have the bill, please?

44
00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:18.221
Your turn. Say: Bill.

45
00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:21.812
Bill.

46
00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:23.621
Specialty.

47
00:02:24.617 --> 00:02:27.650
Specialty means the dish a restaurant is famous for.

48
00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:30.853
The specialty here is Kampot pepper crab.

49
00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:33.940
Your turn. Say: Specialty.

50
00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:37.906
Specialty.

51
00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:39.767
Ambiance.

52
00:02:40.783 --> 00:02:43.479
Ambiance means the feeling or mood of a place.

53
00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:46.245
The ambiance by the river was relaxing.

54
00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:49.653
Your turn. Say: Ambiance.

55
00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:53.687
Ambiance.

56
00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:55.486
Recommend.

57
00:02:56.483 --> 00:02:59.470
Recommend means to say something is good and suggest it.

58
00:03:00.083 --> 00:03:01.375
What do you recommend?

59
00:03:01.983 --> 00:03:04.682
Your turn. Say: Recommend.

60
00:03:07.533 --> 00:03:08.558
Recommend.

61
00:03:09.317 --> 00:03:10.202
Cuisine.

62
00:03:11.217 --> 00:03:14.029
Cuisine means a style of cooking from a country.

63
00:03:14.617 --> 00:03:16.744
Khmer cuisine uses fresh herbs.

64
00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:19.817
Your turn. Say: Cuisine.

65
00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:23.563
Cuisine.

66
00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:27.704
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:30.796
Good evening. Do you have a reservation?

68
00:03:31.883 --> 00:03:35.546
Yes, for two people. Could we see the menu, please?

69
00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:40.347
Of course. I recommend our specialty, pepper crab.

70
00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:45.414
That sounds great. I would like the crab for my main course.

71
00:03:46.517 --> 00:03:47.680
And for dessert?

72
00:03:48.783 --> 00:03:52.771
I would prefer something light. Mango sticky rice, please!

73
00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:55.956
Part three: grammar.

74
00:03:56.817 --> 00:03:59.327
Grammar focus: would like and would prefer.

75
00:03:59.627 --> 00:04:00.826
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:01.517 --> 00:04:03.249
I would like the main course.

77
00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:06.091
I would prefer dessert first.

78
00:04:06.983 --> 00:04:08.495
Would you like some water?

79
00:04:09.433 --> 00:04:13.978
Short form: I'd like, I'd prefer. They are polite ways to say 'I want'.

80
00:04:14.717 --> 00:04:18.379
Be careful! Don't say: I would prefer to dessert first.

81
00:04:20.333 --> 00:04:23.076
Say: I would prefer dessert first.

82
00:04:23.376 --> 00:04:26.397
Use a noun after 'would prefer', or 'to' plus a verb.

83
00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.783
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:31.916
Dinner by the River.

85
00:04:32.216 --> 00:04:35.446
Last Saturday, we made a reservation at a Khmer restaurant.

86
00:04:36.433 --> 00:04:40.383
The waiter recommended the specialty appetizer, fresh spring rolls.

87
00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:45.524
For the main course, my father would like fish amok, and I would prefer chicken curry.

88
00:04:46.533 --> 00:04:49.636
The ambiance by the river was perfect for a family dinner.

89
00:04:50.633 --> 00:04:53.271
After dessert, we paid the bill and left a tip.

90
00:04:54.367 --> 00:04:58.264
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:04:59.117 --> 00:05:00.861
I would blank the fish, please.

92
00:05:01.161 --> 00:05:04.628
A, like. B, liking. C, likes.

93
00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:09.922
The answer is A: like.

94
00:05:11.083 --> 00:05:13.489
Sweet food at the end of a meal is blank.

95
00:05:13.789 --> 00:05:17.129
A, dessert. B, appetizer. C, bill.

96
00:05:20.667 --> 00:05:22.620
The answer is A: dessert.

97
00:05:23.783 --> 00:05:25.992
Booking a table in advance is a blank.

98
00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:30.259
A, reservation. B, tip. C, specialty.

99
00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.730
The answer is A: reservation.

100
00:05:36.933 --> 00:05:40.085
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:43.820
Describe your favorite restaurant and what you order there.

102
00:05:52.617 --> 00:05:54.047
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:54.347 --> 00:06:02.816
My favorite restaurant is a small noodle shop near my school. The ambiance is friendly, and I would always like the beef noodle soup.

104
00:06:03.116 --> 00:06:04.837
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:10.202
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and would like and would prefer.

106
00:06:10.502 --> 00:06:15.523
Today's value is good manners. Say please and thank you, and be polite to everyone.

107
00:06:15.823 --> 00:06:18.336
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

108
00:06:18.636 --> 00:06:22.379
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

